  "id": "Compound::DB01591 - Gene::1133",
  "verbalization": "Solifenacin, a muscarinic acetylcholine receptor antagonist, is shown to bind to Chrm1 and Chrm2, both of which are involved in the G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor activity. This activity is further linked to the participation of Chrm5, suggesting a potential role for Solifenacin in modulating Chrm5 function. The evidence indicates that Solifenacin may influence Chrm5 through a shared pathway involving muscarinic receptors, although the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The high scores in the paths suggest a strong, consistent relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of Solifenacin in the regulation of Chrm5. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Solifenacin in the broader context of muscarinic receptor signaling, though the precise molecular mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
